                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This was quite a pleasant game.\nI've finished the 100 levels in two playthroughs (yes, the 'just one more' thing) in apparently almost 11 hours.\nI've played it on the Deck. I only changed the right trackpad.\n\nTo end the level, you have to fulfill some goals such as clearing certain numbers of colors, destroying specials blocks or getting them to the bottom. Often, there also are blobs, spreading when you don't destroy one.\nThere were a couple of timed levels but I never failed one.\n\nIt felt like the combinations of those features were pretty well done so it never felt like playing the same thing over and over.\n\nI especially liked the levels above 75 as they felt more 'puzzle like'.\nOnly had a handful of nasty levels I had to redo a bunch of times but mostly, they were pretty easy to finish (still fun though). \nIf you don't like the start, restart the level. It's always different.\n\nDuring your play, you can collect coins to buy extra moves when you want to. You can also earn boosters (for example destroy blocks of a chosen color) but I rarely got them but on the other hand, I didn't really need them.\n\nBigger combo's mean more points. You can make it your goal to finish all levels with all stars.",
